  "scope": "Actual packed RN SDK arm64 iOS Simulator Release execution using the existing immutable producer-deleted artifact, without a new Rust export. The original Tauri AppDelegate object is retained. SDK wrappers call its original URL/activity methods first and return their original result; the current engine owns native Linking delivery. Real OS custom URLs pass during background/foreground execution, as repeated identical URLs, after RN removal, and at process startup. The original callback implementations are restored after removal; Tauri still handles the next URL. A test-only file gate delays renderer attachment while the ordinary Tauri app receives a warm URL; the eventual RN event does not become getInitialURL. Cold launch options reach the real RN getInitialURL across renderer replacement and later foreground events. Both cold flows contain no launchApp step; an already-visible app PID is observed afterward. The second app has no native acceptance class and uses unmodified generated startup/default layout. Permissions, stale-continuation retirement, original state/setup, notes, events and native thread/listener cleanup still pass.",
  "universalLinkScope": "The native acceptance button explicitly injects one unrelated NSUserActivity without a webpage URL and one browsing activity. Original Tauri returns NO and YES respectively, emits only the browsing URL, and the SDK preserves those return values without adding a restoration callback. This exercises the real native delegate/Rust plugin/RN path but is not OS associated-domain or live Universal Link acceptance.",
